Lab 19: Implement High Availability for RHACM
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Configure Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management (RHACM) in a high-availability setup across a primary and secondary hub cluster
Implement failover mechanisms and redundancy for RHACM hub components
Test disaster recovery scenarios and validate failover functionality
Build monitoring and automated recovery tooling for a high-availability RHACM environment
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of OpenShift Container Platform concepts
Familiarity with Kubernetes cluster administration and YAML configuration files
Knowledge of RHACM fundamentals and basic operations (hubs, managed clusters, klusterlets)
Understanding of networking concepts including load balancing
Basic knowledge of persistent storage in Kubernetes
